think Council rota lap 12 (last was lap 11, single-stranded.md) -> item 12, active-designing/yonder/20260618-184912_growing-a-language.md. The five moves: stand on proven ground, thin costume first, own the core by path, diverge by strengthening not rewriting, dogfood and gate. This rung stands on proven ground (shape.fill_rect, qoi, color) and diverges by composing, never rewriting a blend or a codec.
think Crux chosen Lindy-first: the DISCRETE sibling of the continuous gradient -- a palette of solid color swatches SEEN on a real image. Highest-Lindy small move: a color picker / scale / legend is a surface every design app shows, and it composes only proven public APIs single-stranded.
think Studied image/shape.rye and image/gradient_paint.rye to match the family idiom exactly: local make_canvas/pixel_at, box bound-checked once up front in u64, the payload validated once before any pixel, refusals by name having painted nothing, QOI round-trip, determinism.
think Design: swatch i spans the integer partition [i*extent/n, (i+1)*extent/n) so cell 0 starts at the first edge and cell n ends at the far edge exactly -- contiguous, disjoint, covering, widths differing by at most one. paint_palette_h and the vertical twin paint_palette_v, bounded to palette_max_swatches 256 so i*extent stays far inside u32.
obs GREEN on the first build and first witness run -- no reds. The uneven case (width 8 over 3 swatches -> widths 2,3,3) proves the partition tiles exactly, the far edge the last swatch; a translucent swatch blends src-over through shape.fill_rect, so the module inherits the blend rather than re-deriving it (single-stranded).
